Vendored Zucchini patch applier

Upstream:  Zucchini, Chromium components/zucchini (The Chromium Authors)
Source:    standalone port https://github.com/rhythmcache/zucchini
           commit 70262b4 ("Update README.md")
License:   BSD 3-Clause, see LICENSE (copied from the port).

Only what applying a patch needs is copied: the apply path, the patch reader,
the DEX and ELF disassemblers (and their helpers), the C API, and the port's
shims for Chromium's base/ headers. The generator, Win32/ZTF disassemblers,
io_utils.cc, tests and build files are not included. Files are copied
unmodified except:

  shim/base/logging.h                 rewritten: log messages are discarded
                                      (no iostream code in the SDK) and a
                                      failed CHECK throws
                                      hands_zucchini::CheckFailure instead of
                                      calling abort().
  shim/base/numerics/safe_conversions.h
                                      FatalLogStream throws the same exception
                                      instead of printing and aborting.
  shim/base/format_macros.h           PRIuS/PRIdS are "zu"/"td" instead of the
                                      MSVC-only "Iu"/"Id".

Why: Android delta patches can carry a Zucchini delta between
archive-patcher's delta-friendly blobs (algorithm
archive-patcher-zucchini-v1+xz). ../hands_zucchini.cc exposes the applier to
ZucchiniDeltaApplier over JNI and turns every failure, including a failed
internal CHECK, into a status code so a bad patch falls back to the full APK
instead of crashing the app.

The patch format must match the generator used by the Hands CLI; update both
from the same upstream revision.
